---
import StudyLayout from "../../../layouts/StudyLayout.astro";

const rows = [
	[
		"Purpose",
		"Supported",
		"01 and the 02.3–02.4 discussion establish compact packing, bulb cockpit, swept aggression and speed rather than a literal insect.",
	],
	[
		"Investigation",
		"Partial",
		"02.1–02.6 provide spatial sketches and a placement workbench. 02.3 and 02.4 drifted into irrelevant detail; the owner explicitly redirected the inquiry. Actual parts and flight are untested.",
	],
	[
		"Alternatives and reasoning",
		"Supported",
		"02.5 reopened whole-ship composition instead of swapping tail appendages. The owner selected 06 / Integrated trident, then adjusted its forward engine cluster in 02.6.",
	],
	[
		"Evidence fit",
		"Partial",
		"Same-scale silhouettes and the screenshot support visual/layout judgments only. Footprint controls and axis guides do not establish full fittings, exhaust clearance or handling.",
	],
	[
		"Cumulative agreement",
		"Supported",
		"The study retains the cockpit decision, rejected body sets, explicit owner correction, exact accepted Trident hull and supplied screenshot. H/A coordinate estimates remain distinguished from exact side settings.",
	],
	[
		"Design coherence",
		"Partial",
		"The owner approved the whole hull and forward packing. Side-footprint overlap, long Scout rail barrels and aft exhaust over the keel remain production-assembly review risks.",
	],
	[
		"Remaining uncertainty",
		"Supported",
		"03 distinguishes prerequisites, reconstructed starting values and human-review gaps. 04 names fitting and flight reviews without inventing their results.",
	],
	[
		"Integration implications",
		"Supported",
		"04 maps shared geometry, coordinate conversion, renderer/nozzles, chassis calculations, collision, selection, saved IDs, canonical Lab, tests and documentation. Implementation has not begun.",
	],
] as const;
---

<StudyLayout>
	<section>
		<h1>Scout — study-quality review</h1>
		<p>
			<a href="/lab/studies/scout-firefly#integration"
				>Return to the study and integration plan</a
			>
		</p>
		<p>
			Agent assessment of this cycle, separate from feasibility, implementation
			authorization and human judgment. Ratings are not averaged.
		</p>
		<div class="table-wrap">
			<table>
				<thead>
					<tr>
						<th>Criterion</th>
						<th>Assessment</th>
						<th>Evidence and gaps</th>
					</tr>
				</thead>
				<tbody>
					{rows.map(([criterion, rating, evidence]) => (
						<tr>
							<th scope="row">{criterion}</th>
							<td>{rating}</td>
							<td>{evidence}</td>
						</tr>
					))}
				</tbody>
			</table>
		</div>
		<h2>Human judgment</h2>
		<p>
			The owner rejected the first 02.2 bodies while retaining the light-bulb
			cockpit, found every 02.3 refinement worse than the original, and called
			out the study’s loss of direction. The owner clarified that the purpose
			was to ideate unknown answers, not demand a reference solution or iterate
			irrelevant details. After the whole-ship reset, 02.5 / 06 was explicitly
			approved. The supplied 02.6 layout was then approved with “this is now
			cool, keep that.” This is design acceptance, not approval of the study
			process as a whole or delivered flight fidelity.
		</p>
		<h2>Automated evidence and limits</h2>
		<p>
			Prior placement-round lint, types and build checks passed. Targeted
			browser checks on the production preview verified sliders, mirrored signs,
			H/A movement, reset, copied coordinates, reference-geometry equality and
			narrow layout. The existing port-4321 dev server failed hydration; the
			fresh production preview on port 4324 worked. These were the
			pre-integration checks, establishing inspectability rather than design
			quality.
		</p>
		<p>
			After separate implementation authorization, the shared Scout was
			delivered in the app and canonical Lab. Added unit/browser checks cover
			exact hull and mount geometry, compact barrels, collision, nozzle
			emission, steering, energy and overspeed, saved builds, every fitting,
			test/survival flow and landscape touch cancellation. Latest full-gate
			results are retained in artifacts/verification/latest.json, separate from
			this quality assessment. Human delivered-fidelity/handling review, device
			performance and deployment are still not claimed.
		</p>
	</section>
</StudyLayout>
<style>
.table-wrap {
	overflow-x: auto;
	margin-block: var(--spacing-lg);
}
table {
	width: 100%;
	border-collapse: collapse;
}
th,
td {
	padding: var(--spacing-sm);
	border-bottom: var(--flight-border);
	text-align: left;
	vertical-align: top;
	line-height: 1.6;
}
</style>
